{"title":"2023 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Really_Simple_Reasoning)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Really Simple Reasoning)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(brute_force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (brute force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(Simple_Visualization)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (Simple Visualization)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CoolMathProblems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CoolMathProblems</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Animated_Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Animated Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_3D_Visualization)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using 3D Visualization)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Magic_Square\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Magic Square</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#A_Correction_and_Concise,_Thorough_Discussion_of_This_Problem_by_Dr._Xue&#39;s_Math_School\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">A Correction and Concise, Thorough Discussion of This Problem by Dr. Xue's Math School</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <i>regular octahedron</i> has eight equilateral triangle faces with four faces meeting at each vertex. Jun will make the regular octahedron shown on the right by folding the piece of paper shown on the left. Which numbered face will end up to the right of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/73573481f96dd080a6118ceb2a3c4588148704dc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] // Diagram by TheMathGuyd import graph; // The Solid // To save processing time, do not use three (dimensions) // Project (roughly) to two size(15cm); pair Fr, Lf, Rt, Tp, Bt, Bk; Lf=(0,0); Rt=(12,1); Fr=(7,-1); Bk=(5,2); Tp=(6,6.7); Bt=(6,-5.2); draw(Lf--Fr--Rt); draw(Lf--Tp--Rt); draw(Lf--Bt--Rt); draw(Tp--Fr--Bt); draw(Lf--Bk--Rt,dashed); draw(Tp--Bk--Bt,dashed); label(rotate(-8.13010235)*slant(0.1)*&quot;$Q$&quot;, (4.2,1.6)); label(rotate(21.8014095)*slant(-0.2)*&quot;$?$&quot;, (8.5,2.05)); pair g = (-8,0); // Define Gap transform real a = 8; draw(g+(-a/2,1)--g+(a/2,1), Arrow()); // Make arrow // Time for the NET pair DA,DB,DC,CD,O; DA = (4*sqrt(3),0); DB = (2*sqrt(3),6); DC = (DA+DB)/3; CD = conj(DC); O=(0,0); transform trf=shift(3g+(0,3)); path NET = O--(-2*DA)--(-2DB)--(-DB)--(2DA-DB)--DB--O--DA--(DA-DB)--O--(-DB)--(-DA)--(-DA-DB)--(-DB); draw(trf*NET); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,trf*DC); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,trf*DC+DA-DB); label(&quot;$5$&quot;,trf*DC-DB); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,trf*DC-DA-DB); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,trf*CD); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,trf*CD-DA); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,trf*CD-DA-DB); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,trf*CD-2DA); [/asy]\" width=\"712\" height=\"258\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4de85cf3f5978446555260f2de6dbc927a7bfac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We color face <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> red and face <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yellow. Note that from the octahedron, face <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and face <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a8960d40d67144344fa86ca431cc1d6491690c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$?$\" width=\"8\" height=\"12\" /> do not share anything in common. From the net, face <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> shares at least one vertex with all other faces except face <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf27edd6ee0c25241392922eca9b9c9144f4d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> which is shown in green: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9be60b3eaaeeab7802d9a0ce9305f176acc62465.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Diagram by TheMathGuyd Edited by MRENTHUSIASM */ import graph; // The Solid // To save processing time, do not use three (dimensions) // Project (roughly) to two size(15cm); pair Fr, Lf, Rt, Tp, Bt, Bk; Lf=(0,0); Rt=(12,1); Fr=(7,-1); Bk=(5,2); Tp=(6,6.7); Bt=(6,-5.2); fill(Tp--Bk--Lf--cycle,red); fill(Bt--Bk--Lf--cycle,green); fill(Fr--Rt--Tp--cycle,yellow); draw(Lf--Fr--Rt); draw(Lf--Tp--Rt); draw(Lf--Bt--Rt); draw(Tp--Fr--Bt); draw(Lf--Bk--Rt,dashed); draw(Tp--Bk--Bt,dashed); label(rotate(-8.13010235)*slant(0.1)*&quot;$Q$&quot;, (4.2,1.6)); label(rotate(21.8014095)*slant(-0.2)*&quot;$?$&quot;, (8.5,2.05)); pair g = (-8,0); // Define Gap transform real a = 8; draw(g+(-a/2,1)--g+(a/2,1), Arrow()); // Make arrow // Time for the NET pair DA,DB,DC,CD,O; DA = (4*sqrt(3),0); DB = (2*sqrt(3),6); DC = (DA+DB)/3; CD = conj(DC); O=(0,0); transform trf=shift(3g+(0,3)); path NET = O--(-2*DA)--(-2DB)--(-DB)--(2DA-DB)--DB--O--DA--(DA-DB)--O--(-DB)--(-DA)--(-DA-DB)--(-DB); fill(trf*((DA-DB)--O--DA--cycle),red); fill(trf*((DA-DB)--O--(-DB)--cycle),yellow); fill(trf*((-2*DA)--(-DA-DB)--(-DA)--cycle),green); draw(trf*NET); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,trf*DC); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,trf*DC+DA-DB); label(&quot;$5$&quot;,trf*DC-DB); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,trf*DC-DA-DB); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,trf*CD); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,trf*CD-DA); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,trf*CD-DA-DB); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,trf*CD-2DA); [/asy]\" width=\"712\" height=\"258\" />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48c462eebec155933ec8a6f08d1ea0f9729daf1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"62\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We label the octohedron going triangle by triangle until we reach the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a8960d40d67144344fa86ca431cc1d6491690c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$?$\" width=\"8\" height=\"12\" /> triangle. The triangle to the left of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> should be labeled with a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Underneath triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The triangle to the right of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and further to the right is triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Finally, the side of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> under triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the triangle to the right of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97b74ee8cccf0c3cfc83d191b525a0059233f3d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the triangles labeled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fc1edcf20b3841d5e15b61e831325707dd22fb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> make the bottom half of the octahedron, as shown below:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/938142dcb5a14e3266ea9764b8bbf41669624d13.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Diagram by TheMathGuyd Edited by MRENTHUSIASM */ import graph; // The Solid // To save processing time, do not use three (dimensions) // Project (roughly) to two size(15cm); pair Fr, Lf, Rt, Tp, Bt, Bk; Lf=(0,0); Rt=(12,1); Fr=(7,-1); Bk=(5,2); Tp=(6,6.7); Bt=(6,-5.2); dot(Bt,linewidth(5)); draw(Lf--Fr--Rt); draw(Lf--Tp--Rt); draw(Lf--Bt--Rt); draw(Tp--Fr--Bt); draw(Lf--Bk--Rt,dashed); draw(Tp--Bk--Bt,dashed); label(rotate(-8.13010235)*slant(0.1)*&quot;$Q$&quot;, (4.2,1.6)); label(rotate(21.8014095)*slant(-0.2)*&quot;$?$&quot;, (8.5,2.05)); pair g = (-8,0); // Define Gap transform real a = 8; draw(g+(-a/2,1)--g+(a/2,1), Arrow()); // Make arrow // Time for the NET pair DA,DB,DC,CD,O; DA = (4*sqrt(3),0); DB = (2*sqrt(3),6); DC = (DA+DB)/3; CD = conj(DC); O=(0,0); transform trf=shift(3g+(0,3)); path NET = O--(-2*DA)--(-2DB)--(-DB)--(2DA-DB)--DB--O--DA--(DA-DB)--O--(-DB)--(-DA)--(-DA-DB)--(-DB); dot(trf*(-DB),linewidth(5)); draw(trf*NET); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,trf*DC); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,trf*DC+DA-DB); label(&quot;$5$&quot;,trf*DC-DB); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,trf*DC-DA-DB); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,trf*CD); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,trf*CD-DA); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,trf*CD-DA-DB); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,trf*CD-2DA); [/asy]\" width=\"712\" height=\"258\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f0100760056ad736cb388cf6916de28fa95bd504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}, \\textbf{(C)}, \\textbf{(D)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> are clearly not the correct answer. Thus, the only choice left is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97b74ee8cccf0c3cfc83d191b525a0059233f3d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />. \n</p><p>~andy_lee\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Really_Simple_Reasoning.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Really_Simple_Reasoning)\">Solution 4 (Really Simple Reasoning)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Really Simple Reasoning)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first half of the octahedron will need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangles connected to one another to form it. We can choose the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and form the half around the vertex they all share. That leaves triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> to form the second half. Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will definitely share its sides with triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, leaving them to share their second side with triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. Since triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> will certainly share its left side with triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the only triangle left to share its right side is triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97b74ee8cccf0c3cfc83d191b525a0059233f3d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~mihikamishra\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28brute_force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(brute_force)\">Solution 5 (brute force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (brute force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Trace the net on your scratch paper, rip it out, and fold it. You'll see the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97b74ee8cccf0c3cfc83d191b525a0059233f3d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> This is not recommended.\n</p><p>~Megacleverstarfish15\n</p>\n<ul><li>extremely unconventional method</li></ul>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28Simple_Visualization.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(Simple_Visualization)\">Video Solution by Math-X (Simple Visualization)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (Simple Visualization)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Ku_c1YHnLt0?si=XilaQFDcnGR8ak7W&amp;t=3364\">https://youtu.be/Ku_c1YHnLt0?si=XilaQFDcnGR8ak7W&amp;t=3364</a> \n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CoolMathProblems\">Video Solution by CoolMathProblems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CoolMathProblems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/t72hL_LiqIM\">https://youtu.be/t72hL_LiqIM</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28A_Clever_Explanation_You.E2.80.99ll_Get_Instantly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zntZrtsnyxc?si=nM5eWOwNU6HRdleZ&amp;t=1699\">https://youtu.be/zntZrtsnyxc?si=nM5eWOwNU6HRdleZ&amp;t=1699</a>\n~hsnacademy\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/tcGcqm5RHiY\">https://youtu.be/tcGcqm5RHiY</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Animated_Video_Solution\">Animated Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Animated Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ECqljkDeA5o\">https://youtu.be/ECqljkDeA5o</a>\n</p><p>~Star League (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://starleague.us\">https://starleague.us</a>)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Using_3D_Visualization.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_3D_Visualization)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using 3D Visualization)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using 3D Visualization)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nVSF2ujZkPE&amp;ab_channel=SohilRathi\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nVSF2ujZkPE&amp;ab_channel=SohilRathi</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Magic_Square\">Video Solution by Magic Square</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Magic Square\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/-N46BeEKaCQ?t=3789\">https://youtu.be/-N46BeEKaCQ?t=3789</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DBqko2xATxs&amp;t=2195\">https://youtu.be/DBqko2xATxs&amp;t=2195</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Dr. David\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RKPKuD-fqLg\">https://youtu.be/RKPKuD-fqLg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"A_Correction_and_Concise.2C_Thorough_Discussion_of_This_Problem_by_Dr._Xue.27s_Math_School\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"A_Correction_and_Concise,_Thorough_Discussion_of_This_Problem_by_Dr._Xue's_Math_School\">A Correction and Concise, Thorough Discussion of This Problem by Dr. Xue's Math School</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: A Correction and Concise, Thorough Discussion of This Problem by Dr. Xue&#39;s Math School\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/aIdo4HQL9O4\">https://youtu.be/aIdo4HQL9O4</a> (this video isn't available anymore)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=atF